   101	))
   102	```
   103	
   104	New work is enforced by this node’s constraints. Its validity enters the recursive chain when the parent, or terminal decider, verifies the node proof.
   105	
   106	The two-self probe performs one combined collapse. It does not implement the hardened canonical disabled-slot construction proposed here, and its self architecture and statement must be rechecked against the completed processor. Its row count is therefore a starting point, not a bound. [`crates/mori-recursion/tests/tree_node_rows.rs:8`; `crates/mori-recursion/tests/tree_node_rows.rs:178`]
   107	
   108	**Do not remove `collapse_self` from `SHKIVC06` as a local optimization.** That collapse currently makes the genesis encoding agree with the host computation. The replacement needs explicit normalization before the accumulator hash, including bases whose scalars have been zeroed. [`crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:538`; `C:verifier/accumulator.rs:387`]
   109	
   110	For arbitrary foreign keys, resolve their key-dependent bases before carrying an obligation onward. A carried dictionary that grows with the number of admitted keys would violate fixed-size recursion. Keep only the fixed self-key scalar set and a bounded number of collapsed points.
   111	
   112	A different SRS requires separate treatment. The KZG verifier parameters contain the SRS-specific G2 element. Do not combine obligations under different SRS values into one pairing equation. Fully verify such foreign proofs in the processor, or implement a separately justified multi-SRS construction. [`P:poly/kzg/params.rs:235`]
   113	
   114	### What cannot presently be claimed
   115	
   116	No evidence establishes a useful **concrete security bound for arbitrary-depth PCD instantiated by this exact construction**. The Lean accumulator model assumes validity preservation by accumulation; it does not prove that cryptographic property. [`clean/fork/Clean/Sherlock/Aggregation.lean:1230`]
   117	
   118	This is an assurance gap, not proof that BLS12-381 PCD is impossible. Closing it requires a composition argument for the chosen transcript, accumulation scheme, self-key binding and adversarial graph construction. Generic recursive-composition analyses can incur substantial depth-dependent loss; stronger results require specified extractor properties and models. [Security Bounds for Proof-Carrying Data](https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/1646.pdf)
