   440	### Constant-size interpretation
   441	
   442	The final verifier checks a fixed-width commitment to the graph and claim set. Opening or enumerating the entire set is a separate operation.
   443	
   444	If “knows exactly which claims” were interpreted as reading every claim during the constant-cost final verification, the requirements would conflict: the verifier cannot read an arbitrarily long list in constant work. The commitment-and-opening interpretation matches GP-2’s explicit requirement that individual claims can be opened. [`D:general-purpose.md:25`; `D:general-purpose.md:47`]
