   517	
   518	Develop the typed claim definitions and formal refinements alongside M1–M4. They must describe the implementation’s continuation and publication boundaries before that implementation is presented as a completed GP milestone.
   519	
   520	Do not freeze final keys after M1 merely because recursion works. Freeze after the processor architecture, complete instruction semantics, statement encoding and decider relation are stable. Subsequent application programs, registry entries and graph shapes must use those keys unchanged.
   521	
   522	### Proposed EARS requirements and design changes
   523	
   524	These are proposed text, not file edits.
   525	
   526	| Proposed requirement | Text |
   527	|---|---|
   528	| **GP-MEM** | The processor SHALL authenticate every program, input and mutable-memory access against committed storage. Storage capacity SHALL NOT depend on a proving key. |
   529	| **GP-INIT** | Before the processor publishes a run segment as originating at height zero, it SHALL prove canonical initialization from the committed program, input and execution parameters. |
   530	| **GP-FOREIGN** | When a foreign proof is consumed, the processor SHALL authenticate its complete verifier interpretation and statement adapter against an authorized registry commitment. |
   531	| **GP-FORMAT** | When a claim asserts compatibility with a ledger proof format, the processor SHALL enforce that format’s transcript, encodings, instance layout and complete parsing rules. |
   532	| **GP-SHAPE** | Every decided root SHALL bind the typed dependency graph and local work into its public statement. |
   533	| **GP-DAG** | The processor SHALL permit a verified claim to feed multiple consumers. It SHALL prevent that reuse from duplicating execution coverage or settlement effects. |
   534	| **GP-COMPLETE** | The decider SHALL refuse a root containing an unfinished initialization, memory, verifier, adapter or claim-set operation. |
   535	| **GP-KEYS** | Changing a program, input, memory capacity, registry entry, graph shape or graph depth SHALL NOT require a different processor or decider key. |
   536	
   537	Replace D4 and §§2.3–2.4 with the bounded processor and committed-memory design. Replace §3.1 with binary PCD. Extend §3.3 to typed terminal claims. Replace §3.6’s single-program segment model with typed composition while retaining segment linkage as a subrelation. Rewrite SRC-013/014 around processor work per proof, rather than a finite family or fixed-capacity carrier. [`D:design.md:12`; `D:design.md:46`; `D:design.md:70`; `D:design.md:114`; `D:requirements.md:35`]
