Named lifts do not inherently require a fork: the public API exposes accumulator encodings and lets a circuit assign a replacement with chosen names. Every replacement lane would need a constraint linking it to the original accumulator. I also confirmed that the 730,243-row probe lacks the proposed slot hardening, so it does not yet establish N’s fit. (`MC:verifier/verifier_gadget.rs:112,160`; `MC:verifier/accumulator.rs:280`; `crates/mori-recursion/tests/tree_node_rows.rs:178`)
