     1	//! Versioned physical lane view of the generic C6 machine root and frame stack.
     2	//!
     3	//! Profile `sherlock-c6-phys/1` (C6P1), Chunk 1: one root+frames image section,
     4	//! plus owned recorders around the existing fixed owner step for A135
     5	//! (`KMachinePushAccept`) and A140 (`KMachinePushRefuse`).
     6	//!
     7	//! This module is a codec and an owned-record consumer. It does not admit
     8	//! programs, construct `Admitted`/`MachineImage`, select rules, evaluate, or step
     9	//! twice. The section carries no program binding, helper, result, task, data,
    10	//! env-cell or value-slot table; those are Chunk 3/4 and remain OPEN. No native,
    11	//! proof, encoder-conformance or full-state physical POST claim is made.
    12	//!
    13	//! Layout (lane offsets are the `L_*` constants): magic, version, 17-lane
    14	//! control, control origin, 2-lane env root, stack limit, 3-lane outcome,
    15	//! six u128 counters, alloc(3), active(4), seg active(4), seg alloc(3), seg
    16	//! consumed work, frame count; then `frame_count` 13-lane frames bottom-to-top.
    17	//!
    18	//! `decode_image_section` first-error precedence:
    19	//! 1. fewer than 48 lanes: `Truncated`; 2. `BadMagic`; 3. `BadVersion`;
    20	//! 4. control record, structurally, ascending lanes (record-relative lane
    21	//!    numbers; an embedded frame reports section "frame");
    22	//! 5. root lanes 19..=47 structurally in ascending lane order (usize/u8
    23	//!    representability, env/outcome/ref tags, padding; section-absolute lanes);
    24	//! 6. representation caps: control, then root fields in lane order, then the
    25	//!    frame count against `max_frames`;
    26	//! 7. exact length: `Truncated`, then `TrailingLanes` (no allocation before);
    27	//! 8. frames bottom-to-top, each structurally then against caps.
    28	//! Indices must be strictly below their table cap; counts at most their cap;
    29	//! a slice is checked for end overflow, then arity, then end <= table cap.
    30	//! Builtin TypeId exception: the five TypeId index fields (ReturnF.return_type,
    31	//! ConstructorFieldsF.type_id and .field_type, Bound.return_type,
    32	//! Materialize.type_id) are checked against the effective cap
    33	//! `max(max_types, 4)`, because builtin TypeIds 0..=3 exist even when
    34	//! `type_rows < 4` (owner SI-15 `types.len().max(4)`; dedicated
    35	//! `check_program_view` uses 4 types). `max_types` itself stays the declared
    36	//! `type_rows` and still caps the program `types`/`type_args` table counts.
    37	//! `AllocCounters::data_fields`/`ActiveLengths::data_fields` have no caps field
    38	//! and are carried exactly. Membership of nominal IDs in admitted tables is
    39	//! cross-section work (Chunk 4) and is not claimed.
