Two more boundaries need explicit treatment. An adapter that only prepares an inner proof and resolves its bases must carry that inner accumulator onward or check its pairing; verifying the adapter proof alone does not discharge it. Also, hashing `JOIN(left,right)` binds ordered composition, but does not by itself provide duplicate-free set semantics or replay protection across different groupings. (`MC:verifier/verifier_gadget.rs:683`; `fable/design-1.md:267,295,329`)
